Private Discuss: FrameCryptor uses the raw key material (no PBKDF2 / HKDF derivation).

The web client (discuss-rooms e2ee.worker) and the native Discuss apps encrypt media frames
with the 32-byte AES-256-GCM key exactly as exchanged (RSA-OAEP wrapped). Upstream LiveKit
derives a 128-bit key from that material, which cannot interoperate. Only the two frame paths
change (encryptFrame / decryptFrame); DataPacketCryptor is untouched. The ratchet fallback
never runs with ratchetWindowSize = 0. Applied to apple_prefixed and android_prefixed.

